:"The guide separates clean paper/cardboard from tissues and food-soiled paper.","zh":"指引将干净纸板与纸巾、食品污染纸类区分处理。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-sorting"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"Victoria teaching example. Follow the stated service conditions; local council rules may differ.","zh":"Victoria 教学示例。按题目说明的服务条件判断；各 council 规则可能不同。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["intermediate-clean-streams"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"i-clean-sticker","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"intermediate","topicCode":"clean-streams","prompt":{"en":"Your FOGO service accepts fruit scraps. What should you remove from a peel first?","zh":"你的 FOGO 服务接受水果残余。投放果皮前应先去掉什么？"},"options":[{"optionId":"nothing","label":{"en":"Nothing; packaging breaks down with food","zh":"不必去掉，包装会和食物一起分解"}},{"optionId":"peel","label":{"en":"Add a bag to keep the peel contained","zh":"加一个袋子装住果皮"}},{"optionId":"sticker","label":{"en":"The produce sticker and packaging","zh":"水果贴纸与包装"}}],"correctOptionId":"sticker","explanation":{"en":"Non-food items can contaminate organic collections.","zh":"非食物物品可能污染有机物收集。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-fogo"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"Victoria teaching example. Follow the stated service conditions; local council rules may differ.","zh":"Victoria 教学示例。按题目说明的服务条件判断；各 council 规则可能不同。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["intermediate-clean-streams"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"i-local-soft","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"intermediate","topicCode":"local-collection","prompt":{"en":"No household soft-plastic collection is confirmed. What should you check?","zh":"尚未确认家用软塑料收集服务。应该核对什么？"},"options":[{"optionId":"colour","label":{"en":"Use its plastic code as confirmation","zh":"用塑料编号确认"}},{"optionId":"service","label":{"en":"An active local collection or drop-off service","zh":"当地正在运行的收集或投放服务"}},{"optionId":"old","label":{"en":"Assume an old supermarket scheme still operates","zh":"认为以前的超市收集一直有效"}}],"correctOptionId":"service","explanation":{"en":"Soft-plastic arrangements change. Verify an active service instead of relying on old advice.","zh":"软塑料收集安排会变化，应核实有效服务，而不是沿用旧建议。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-sorting"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"Victoria teaching example. Follow the stated service conditions; local council rules may differ.","zh":"Victoria 教学示例。按题目说明的服务条件判断；各 council 规则可能不同。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["intermediate-local-guide"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"i-local-glass","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"intermediate","topicCode":"local-collection","prompt":{"en":"Your council provides a separate glass service for jars. Where should an accepted empty jar go?","zh":"当地 council 为玻璃罐提供单独收集服务。符合要求的空玻璃罐应该去哪里？"},"options":[{"optionId":"glass","label":{"en":"The separate glass service","zh":"单独玻璃收集服务"}},{"optionId":"mixed","label":{"en":"Mixed recycling regardless of instructions","zh":"无视说明投入混合回收"}},{"optionId":"fogo","label":{"en":"Food organics","zh":"厨余"}}],"correctOptionId":"glass","explanation":{"en":"Use the separate service specified; it helps protect other recyclables from broken glass.","zh":"按题目指定的单独服务处理，有助于防止碎玻璃污染其他回收物。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-glass"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"Victoria teaching example. Follow the stated service conditions; local council rules may differ.","zh":"Victoria 教学示例。按题目说明的服务条件判断；各 council 规则可能不同。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["intermediate-local-guide"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"i-local-deposit","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"intermediate","topicCode":"local-collection","prompt":{"en":"Before taking a drink container for a CDS Vic refund, what should you verify?","zh":"把饮料容器带去 CDS Vic 退费前，应核对什么？"},"options":[{"optionId":"all","label":{"en":"Assume every glass container qualifies","zh":"认为所有玻璃容器都符合"}},{"optionId":"size","label":{"en":"Check its material only","zh":"只查看材质"}},{"optionId":"eligible","label":{"en":"Its eligibility and a current refund point","zh":"容器资格与有效退费点"}}],"correctOptionId":"eligible","explanation":{"en":"The scheme covers eligible drink containers; not every container qualifies.","zh":"该计划只接受符合条件的饮料容器，并非所有容器都可以退费。"},"sourceRefs":["cds-vic"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"Victoria teaching example. Follow the stated service conditions; local council rules may differ.","zh":"Victoria 教学示例。按题目说明的服务条件判断；各 council 规则可能不同。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["intermediate-local-guide"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"i-local-baking-glass","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"intermediate","topicCode":"local-collection","prompt":{"en":"Can a glass baking dish be treated like an accepted glass drink bottle in Victoria''s bottle/jar recycling?","zh":"在 Victoria 的瓶罐玻璃回收中，玻璃烤盘可以和符合要求的饮料瓶一样处理吗？"},"options":[{"optionId":"unbroken","label":{"en":"Yes, if it is unbroken and empty","zh":"可以，只要它完整且已倒空"}},{"optionId":"different","label":{"en":"No; check the disposal route for that item","zh":"不可以；查看该物品的处理方式"}},{"optionId":"same","label":{"en":"Yes; all glass is the same for collection","zh":"可以，所有玻璃的收集方式相同"}}],"correctOptionId":"different","explanation":{"en":"Heat-resistant glassware differs from container glass; the bottle/jar stream is not suitable.","zh":"耐热玻璃器具不同于瓶罐玻璃，不适合瓶罐回收流。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-sorting"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"Victoria teaching example. Follow the stated service conditions; local council rules may differ.","zh":"Victoria 教学示例。按题目说明的服务条件判断；各 council 规则可能不同。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["intermediate-local-guide"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"i-reuse-bag","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"intermediate","topicCode":"reuse-resources","prompt":{"en":"You already own a usable reusable shopping bag. Which action avoids more single-use waste?","zh":"你已有一个可用的购物袋。哪种做法能减少一次性废弃物？"},"options":[{"optionId":"reuse","label":{"en":"Bring it and use it again","zh":"带上并继续使用"}},{"optionId":"replace","label":{"en":"Buy a new reusable bag every trip","zh":"每次购物都买一个新环保袋"}},{"optionId":"leave-home","label":{"en":"Leave it at home and take a new checkout bag","zh":"把它留在家里，结账时另拿购物袋"}}],"correctOptionId":"reuse","explanation":{"en":"Repeated use makes the reusable item replace additional single-use items.","zh":"反复使用才能让可重复使用物品替代更多一次性物品。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-single-use"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"No local disposal instruction is implied.","zh":"本题不代表当地投放指引。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["intermediate-components"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"i-reuse-jar","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"intermediate","topicCode":"reuse-resources","prompt":{"en":"When reusing a container for food, what matters most?","zh":"将容器重复用于盛装食物时，最重要的是什么？"},"options":[{"optionId":"appearance","label":{"en":"It looks attractive, regardless of previous contents","zh":"外观漂亮即可，不看原先装什么"}},{"optionId":"rinse-only","label":{"en":"A rinse makes any container suitable for food","zh":"冲洗一下就能让任何容器适合盛装食品"}},{"optionId":"suitable","label":{"en":"It is clean and suitable for that food use","zh":"它干净且适合这种食品用途"}}],"correctOptionId":"suitable","explanation":{"en":"Reuse must be safe and suitable; avoid repurposing containers into unsafe uses.","zh":"重复使用应安全、合适，不能让容器承担不安全的用途。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-reuse"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"No local disposal instruction is implied.","zh":"本题不代表当地投放指引。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["intermediate-components"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"i-reuse-clean-stream","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"intermediate","topicCode":"reuse-resources","prompt":{"en":"Why can separating accepted glass from mixed recycling help other materials?","zh":"为什么将可接受的玻璃与混合回收分开，有助于其他材料？"},"options":[{"optionId":"erase","label":{"en":"It removes the need to check local services","zh":"不再需要查看当地服务"}},{"optionId":"protect","label":{"en":"It reduces broken glass contaminating paper and plastic","zh":"减少碎玻璃混入纸类与塑料"}},{"optionId":"count","label":{"en":"It counts every jar as a new product immediately","zh":"立即把每个罐子算成新产品"}}],"correctOptionId":"protect","explanation":{"en":"A cleaner stream makes recovery easier; separation itself is not proof a new product was made.","zh":"更干净的收集流有助于回收；完成分离不等于已经制成新产品。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-glass"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"Victoria teaching example. Follow the stated service conditions; local council rules may differ.","zh":"Victoria 教学示例。按题目说明的服务条件判断；各 council 规则可能不同。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["intermediate-clean-streams"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"i-reuse-donate","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"intermediate","topicCode":"reuse-resources","prompt":{"en":"You no longer need a reusable lunch container. What is a suitable reuse option?","zh":"你不再需要一个可重复使用的饭盒。哪种再利用方式合适？"},"options":[{"optionId":"safe","label":{"en":"Offer it only if clean, safe and usable","zh":"只在干净、安全、可用时转给别人"}},{"optionId":"damaged","label":{"en":"Donate it even if damaged and unsafe","zh":"损坏、不安全也捐出"}},{"optionId":"mixed","label":{"en":"Place it in mixed recycling without checking","zh":"不核对就投入混合回收"}}],"correctOptionId":"safe","explanation":{"en":"Only pass on items suitable for someone else to use.","zh":"只应转交适合他人继续使用的物品。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-reuse"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"No local disposal instruction is implied.","zh":"本题不代表当地投放指引。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["intermediate-components"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-plan-stocktake","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"planning","prompt":{"en":"Before making a shopping list, which check best prevents duplicate purchases?","zh":"写购物清单前，哪项检查最能避免重复购买？"},"options":[{"optionId":"only-price","label":{"en":"Check only discounts","zh":"只查看折扣"}},{"optionId":"replace","label":{"en":"List replacements from memory","zh":"凭记忆列出要补买的食物"}},{"optionId":"all-storage","label":{"en":"Check fridge, freezer and pantry","zh":"查看冰箱、冷冻室和储物柜"}}],"correctOptionId":"all-storage","explanation":{"en":"A stocktake across storage areas reveals what you already have.","zh":"查看各储存区域能了解已有食物。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-planning"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-plan-first"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-plan-use-soon","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"planning","prompt":{"en":"You have vegetables that need using soon and remain safe. Which meal plan fits best?","zh":"你有一些仍安全、但需要尽快使用的蔬菜。哪种餐食计划最好？"},"options":[{"optionId":"later","label":{"en":"Wait until all new groceries are finished","zh":"先吃完全部新买的食物再考虑"}},{"optionId":"use-existing","label":{"en":"Choose a meal using those vegetables","zh":"选择能用到这些蔬菜的一餐"}},{"optionId":"new-recipe","label":{"en":"Buy different vegetables for every recipe","zh":"每道菜都另买新蔬菜"}}],"correctOptionId":"use-existing","explanation":{"en":"Planning around existing ingredients reduces the chance they are forgotten.","zh":"围绕已有食材计划餐食，能减少遗忘。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-planning"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-plan-first"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-plan-portions","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"planning","prompt":{"en":"Two people will be away tonight. What should change in your dinner plan?","zh":"今晚有两个人不在家吃饭。应如何调整晚餐计划？"},"options":[{"optionId":"adjust","label":{"en":"Adjust portions for those who will eat","zh":"按实际就餐人数调整份量"}},{"optionId":"usual","label":{"en":"Cook the usual portions with no leftover plan","zh":"照常做且不安排剩菜用途"}},{"optionId":"extra","label":{"en":"Add extra portions because ingredients are available","zh":"有食材就增加份量"}}],"correctOptionId":"adjust","explanation":{"en":"Matching portions to attendance helps avoid unwanted leftovers.","zh":"按就餐人数安排份量，有助于避免多余剩菜。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-planning"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-plan-first"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-plan-offer","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"planning","prompt":{"en":"A bulk offer costs less per unit, but you cannot use it safely in time. What best prevents waste?","zh":"大包装单价更低，但你无法及时安全用完。怎样更能避免浪费？"},"options":[{"optionId":"unit-price","label":{"en":"Choose the biggest pack for its unit price","zh":"只看单价，选最大包装"}},{"optionId":"bin-later","label":{"en":"Buy it and decide what to discard later","zh":"先买，再决定扔哪些"}},{"optionId":"need","label":{"en":"Buy only an amount you can use","zh":"只买能用完的量"}}],"correctOptionId":"need","explanation":{"en":"A lower unit price does not make unused food useful; plan quantities you can use.","zh":"单价低不等于食物能被用掉，应按可使用的数量购买。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-planning"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-plan-first"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-plan-shared-ingredient","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"planning","prompt":{"en":"A recipe uses half a tub of an ingredient. What makes a useful plan for the remainder?","zh":"一道菜只用半盒食材。怎样安排剩下部分更有帮助？"},"options":[{"optionId":"untracked","label":{"en":"Leave it unlabelled at the back","zh":"不做记录，放到后面"}},{"optionId":"second-meal","label":{"en":"Plan another meal using it within safe storage limits","zh":"在安全储存期限内安排另一餐使用"}},{"optionId":"buy-another","label":{"en":"Buy another tub for the next recipe","zh":"下道菜再买一盒"}}],"correctOptionId":"second-meal","explanation":{"en":"Linking meals around shared ingredients gives the remainder a purpose.","zh":"让不同餐食共用食材，可为剩余部分安排用途。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-planning"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-plan-first"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-plan-change","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"planning","prompt":{"en":"Your week''s plans change after shopping. What is the best next step?","zh":"购物后本周安排改变了。下一步怎样做最好？"},"options":[{"optionId":"review","label":{"en":"Review perishables and update meals or safe storage plans","zh":"查看易腐食物，调整餐食或安全储存安排"}},{"optionId":"ignore","label":{"en":"Keep the original plan without checking food","zh":"不查看食物，照原计划放着"}},{"optionId":"new-shop","label":{"en":"Start a new shop before checking existing food","zh":"还没看已有食物就重新购物"}}],"correctOptionId":"review","explanation":{"en":"A flexible plan keeps existing food visible when routines change.","zh":"安排改变时，灵活调整能让已有食物继续被关注。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-planning","vic-storage"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-plan-first"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-storage-use-by","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"storage-safety","prompt":{"en":"A food is past its use-by date. It smells normal. What should you do?","zh":"食物已过 use-by 日期，但闻起来正常。应该怎么办？"},"options":[{"optionId":"smell","label":{"en":"Use smell alone to decide it is safe","zh":"只凭气味判定安全"}},{"optionId":"relabel","label":{"en":"Cook it longer to override the date","zh":"延长烹饪时间以替代日期限制"}},{"optionId":"do-not-eat","label":{"en":"Do not eat it","zh":"不要食用"}}],"correctOptionId":"do-not-eat","explanation":{"en":"Use-by is a safety limit. Smell does not override it.","zh":"Use-by 是安全期限，气味不能替代这一限制。"},"sourceRefs":["fsanz-dates","fsanz-safety"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-storage"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-storage-best-before","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"storage-safety","prompt":{"en":"What does a best-before date mainly describe?","zh":"Best-before 日期主要说明什么？"},"options":[{"optionId":"opened","label":{"en":"The day the pack was opened","zh":"包装被打开的日期"}},{"optionId":"quality","label":{"en":"Expected food quality","zh":"预期食品品质"}},{"optionId":"same","label":{"en":"The same safety cutoff as use-by","zh":"与 use-by 相同的安全截止"}}],"correctOptionId":"quality","explanation":{"en":"Best-before concerns quality. Storage instructions and food condition still matter.","zh":"Best-before 主要涉及品质，仍需注意储存说明和食物状态。"},"sourceRefs":["fsanz-dates"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-storage"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-storage-label","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"storage-safety","prompt":{"en":"A label says keep refrigerated after opening. What should you follow?","zh":"标签要求开封后冷藏。应怎样做？"},"options":[{"optionId":"label","label":{"en":"Follow that storage instruction","zh":"遵循这项储存要求"}},{"optionId":"date-only","label":{"en":"Use the date alone regardless of storage","zh":"只看日期，不考虑储存"}},{"optionId":"room","label":{"en":"Keep it on the counter to remember it","zh":"为了记得使用而放在室温台面"}}],"correctOptionId":"label","explanation":{"en":"Date marks rely on appropriate storage; follow the product''s instructions.","zh":"日期标记以适当储存为前提，应遵循产品说明。"},"sourceRefs":["fsanz-dates"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-storage"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-storage-thaw","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"storage-safety","prompt":{"en":"How should frozen perishable food be thawed according to FSANZ?","zh":"按 FSANZ 指引，冷冻易腐食物应如何解冻？"},"options":[{"optionId":"counter","label":{"en":"At room temperature all day","zh":"在室温下放一整天"}},{"optionId":"sun","label":{"en":"Move it to a warm spot to speed thawing","zh":"移到温暖处加快解冻"}},{"optionId":"cold","label":{"en":"In the fridge or using a microwave","zh":"在冰箱里或使用微波炉"}}],"correctOptionId":"cold","explanation":{"en":"Avoid room-temperature thawing; use the fridge or microwave as instructed.","zh":"避免室温解冻，按指引使用冰箱或微波炉。"},"sourceRefs":["fsanz-safety"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-storage"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-priority-prevent","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"prevention-priority","prompt":{"en":"You can either buy less surplus food or improve sorting of the surplus later. Which prevents the waste first?","zh":"可以少买多余食物，也可以事后更好地分类多余食物。哪项先预防浪费？"},"options":[{"optionId":"package","label":{"en":"Change the surplus food''s packaging","zh":"更换多余食物的包装"}},{"optionId":"less","label":{"en":"Buy only what you can use","zh":"只买能使用的食物"}},{"optionId":"sort","label":{"en":"Buy the surplus and sort it later","zh":"先买多余食物，再分类"}}],"correctOptionId":"less","explanation":{"en":"Prevention avoids creating the surplus; sorting deals with it after it exists.","zh":"预防减少多余食物的产生；分类是在产生之后处理。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-planning"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-plan-first"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-priority-safe-reuse","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"prevention-priority","prompt":{"en":"Which is a sensible way to reduce packaging waste at lunch?","zh":"哪种做法能合理减少午餐包装废弃物？"},"options":[{"optionId":"suitable","label":{"en":"Use an existing clean, food-suitable reusable container","zh":"使用已有、干净、适合食品的可重复使用容器"}},{"optionId":"rinse-any","label":{"en":"Rinse any available container without checking food suitability","zh":"冲洗任意现有容器，不查看是否适合盛装食品"}},{"optionId":"single-use","label":{"en":"Buy single-use packs labelled recyclable for each lunch","zh":"每餐购买标有可回收的一次性包装"}}],"correctOptionId":"suitable","explanation":{"en":"Useful reuse combines repeated use with safety and suitability.","zh":"有效再利用兼顾重复使用、安全和适用性。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-reuse","vic-single-use"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["intermediate-components"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-priority-fogo","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"prevention-priority","prompt":{"en":"What can a suitable FOGO service do for unavoidable food scraps?","zh":"合适的 FOGO 服务可以怎样处理无法避免的食物残余？"},"options":[{"optionId":"all-packaging","label":{"en":"Collect all food packaging with the scraps","zh":"将所有食品包装与残余一起收集"}},{"optionId":"replace-plan","label":{"en":"Replace meal planning by composting unused food","zh":"将未用食物堆肥，以此替代餐食计划"}},{"optionId":"compost","label":{"en":"Collect them for composting","zh":"收集它们用于堆肥"}}],"correctOptionId":"compost","explanation":{"en":"Organics collection helps handle scraps, while avoiding edible waste remains a separate goal.","zh":"有机物收集有助于处理残余；避免可食用食物浪费仍是另一项目标。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-fogo","unfccc-2024"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-climate"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-priority-scrap-vs-food","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"prevention-priority","prompt":{"en":"Which plan addresses both prevention and unavoidable scraps?","zh":"哪种计划兼顾预防浪费与无法避免的残余？"},"options":[{"optionId":"all-bin","label":{"en":"Treat usable food and packaging as one waste item","zh":"把可用食物与包装当成同一废弃物"}},{"optionId":"both","label":{"en":"Use edible ingredients, then check an accepted route for scraps","zh":"先使用可食用食材，再核对残余的接收方式"}},{"optionId":"all-compost","label":{"en":"Send usable ingredients and scraps directly to compost","zh":"把可用食材和残余都直接堆肥"}}],"correctOptionId":"both","explanation":{"en":"Use edible food where safe; separately route unavoidable scraps through an accepted service.","zh":"在安全前提下使用可食用食物，再单独按合适服务处理无法避免的残余。"},"sourceRefs":["vic-planning","vic-fogo"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"AU-VIC","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-climate"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-evidence-range","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"climate-evidence","prompt":{"en":"UNFCCC''s 8–10% estimate refers to which scope?","zh":"UNFCCC 的 8–10% 估计对应哪个范围？"},"options":[{"optionId":"global","label":{"en":"Annual global greenhouse gas emissions linked to food loss and waste","zh":"与食物损失及浪费有关的全球年度温室气体排放"}},{"optionId":"household","label":{"en":"Only emissions from household food bins","zh":"仅家庭厨余桶产生的排放"}},{"optionId":"personal","label":{"en":"This learner''s personal emissions reduction","zh":"本学习者的个人减排量"}}],"correctOptionId":"global","explanation":{"en":"The estimate combines food loss and waste globally, not a personal saving.","zh":"该估计涵盖全球食物损失与浪费，并非个人节省量。"},"sourceRefs":["unfccc-2024"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"global","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-climate"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-evidence-year","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"climate-evidence","prompt":{"en":"A report released in 2024 estimates food waste in 2022. Which year belongs with the measured amount?","zh":"2024 年发布的报告估计了 2022 年食物浪费量。统计数值应注明哪一年？"},"options":[{"optionId":"publication","label":{"en":"2024 only","zh":"只标 2024 年"}},{"optionId":"current","label":{"en":"The current app year","zh":"当前 App 使用年份"}},{"optionId":"measurement","label":{"en":"2022, with 2024 as the publication year","zh":"2022 年，并另注明 2024 年发布"}}],"correctOptionId":"measurement","explanation":{"en":"The observation period and publication date are different fields.","zh":"统计时期与发布日期是不同字段。"},"sourceRefs":["unep-index-2024"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"global","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-climate"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-evidence-sectors","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"climate-evidence","prompt":{"en":"The UNEP 2022 estimate of 1.05 billion tonnes covers which sectors?","zh":"UNEP 对 2022 年 10.5 亿吨食物废弃物的估计涵盖哪些领域？"},"options":[{"optionId":"farms","label":{"en":"Farms only","zh":"仅农场"}},{"optionId":"sectors","label":{"en":"Retail, food service and households","zh":"零售、餐饮服务和家庭"}},{"optionId":"homes","label":{"en":"Households only","zh":"仅家庭"}}],"correctOptionId":"sectors","explanation":{"en":"This estimate covers those three consumer-level sectors and includes inedible parts.","zh":"该估计涵盖这三个消费端领域，并包含不可食用部分。"},"sourceRefs":["unep-index-2024"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"global","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-climate"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-evidence-sdg","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"climate-evidence","prompt":{"en":"Which activity most directly fits SDG 13.3 in this app?","zh":"本 App 中哪项活动最直接对应 SDG 13.3？"},"options":[{"optionId":"learn","label":{"en":"Learning how waste relates to climate and reflecting on action","zh":"学习浪费与气候的关系并思考行动"}},{"optionId":"sorting-only","label":{"en":"Counting returned containers without climate learning","zh":"只统计退回容器数量，不涉及气候学习"}},{"optionId":"carbon-score","label":{"en":"Using the quiz score as a personal carbon reduction figure","zh":"把测验成绩当作个人减排数值"}}],"correctOptionId":"learn","explanation":{"en":"The app contributes educational content; it does not certify UN indicators.","zh":"App 提供教育内容，不认证联合国指标。"},"sourceRefs":["sdg13"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"global","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-climate"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-evidence-result","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"climate-evidence","prompt":{"en":"What can a completed waste quiz demonstrate on its own?","zh":"单凭完成一次 waste 测验，能说明什么？"},"options":[{"optionId":"tonnes","label":{"en":"Measured tonnes of food saved","zh":"已测量的食物节省吨数"}},{"optionId":"carbon","label":{"en":"A verified personal carbon reduction","zh":"经过验证的个人减排量"}},{"optionId":"learning","label":{"en":"A recorded learning result","zh":"一项已记录的学习结果"}}],"correctOptionId":"learning","explanation":{"en":"A score records assessment performance. Environmental outcomes require separate evidence.","zh":"成绩记录测验表现；环境效果需要另行取得证据。"},"sourceRefs":["sdg13","unfccc-2024"],"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","regionCode":"global","serviceAssumptions":{"en":"A teaching scenario; no personal emissions saving or council service is assumed.","zh":"教学情景；不预设个人减排量或当地收集服务。"},"relatedActivityCodes":["advanced-climate"],"imageAssetKey":null,"status":"active"},{"questionCode":"a-evidence-resources","revision":1,"contentVersion":"learning-room-v1","stageCode":"advanced","topicCode":"climate-evidence","prompt":{"en":"Why does food waste matter before it reaches a bin?","zh":"为什么食物还未进入垃圾桶，浪费就已涉及环境问题？"},"options":[{"optionId":"packaging-only","label":{"en":"Only packaging has used resources","zh":"只有包装消耗了资源"}},{"optionId":"inputs","label":{"en":"Growing and 